<para id="RM0000005KY00RX" category="C" type-id="3007N" name-id="5226X-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>B1411/11</dtccode>
<dtcname>Room temperature sensor malfunction</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM0000005KY00RX_05" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000AIG00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The cooler thermistor (room temperature sensor) is installed in the instrument panel, detects the cabin temperature and is used for "AUTO" control of the heater &amp; air conditioner. The resistance of the cooler thermistor (room temperature sensor) changes in accordance with changes in cabin temperature: as the cabin temperature decreases, the resistance increases, and as the cabin temperature increases, the resistance decreases. The air conditioner amplifier assembly outputs a voltage (5V) to the cooler thermistor (room temperature sensor) and reads the voltage changes that accompany changes in the cooler thermistor resistance.</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3" align="left">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="3.08in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
