<subpara id="RM0000005KY00RX_07" type-id="51" category="05">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000005KY00RX_08" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM0000005KY00RX_08_0008" proc-id="RM0550J___0000AII00000">
<testtitle>Read TaSCAN Data (Room Temperature Sensor)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), inspect the ECU Data Monitor by following the screen instructions.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt/>
</specitem>
<table pgwide="1">
<title>[System selection screen: Body → A/C → ECU Data Monitor]</title>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.50in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.50in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="3.08in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Item Name</ptxt>
<ptxt>[Item Symbol]</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Reference Value</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Room Temperature Sensor</ptxt>
<ptxt>[THI]</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>-</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Displayed in range -6.5 to 57.25°C</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When open: (-6.5°C) displayed</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When shorted: (57.25°C) displayed</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
<table>
<title>Result</title>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.04in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.09in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Does not display same value as cooler thermistor (room temperature sensor) ambient temperature</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Displays same value as cooler thermistor (room temperature sensor) ambient temperature</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000005KY00RX_08_0009" fin="false">A</down>
<right ref="RM0000005KY00RX_08_0011" fin="true">B</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000005KY00RX_08_0009" proc-id="RM0550J___0000AIJ00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Cooler Thermistor (Room Temperature Sensor)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the cooler thermistor (room temperature sensor) connector.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the terminals of the connector.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E105412J05" width="2.775699831in" height="4.7836529in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.37in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
<ptxt>[Ambient Temperature]</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry morerows="10" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1(+) - 2(-)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>10°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>3.00 to 3.73 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>15°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>2.45 to 2.88 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>20°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1.95 to 2.30 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>25°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1.60 to 1.80 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>30°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1.28 to 1.47 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>35°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1.00 to 1.22 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>40°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>0.80 to 1.00 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>45°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>0.65 to 0.85 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>50°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>0.50 to 0.70 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>55°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>0.44 to 0.60 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>60°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>0.36 to 0.50 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Touching the temperature sensor part will affect it with body heat and prevent a correct judgment, so hold the connector side when inspecting the sensor.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Allow the sensor to adjust to the ambient temperature before inspecting.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000005KY00RX_08_0010" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM0000005KY00RX_08_0012" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000005KY00RX_08_0010" proc-id="RM0550J___0000AIK00000">
